<WRAP center round info 60%>
Attention! If your device has too recent official firmware (6.5 or newer), you need to downgrade the official firmware first, see below. You can tell it is not working if the last dd commands are completed under 10 seconds (30s+ are expected).
If your AP is already adoptet from your UniFi Network Application, you can downgrade with that. After that you have to "remove" it, than you can connect via ssh.
</WRAP>
<WRAP center round info 60%>
If this is done in a network with DHCP server present, the IP address of the device will be assigned.
</WRAP>

Connect to the booted device at 192.168.1.20 using username/password "ubnt". <code>ssh ubnt@192.168.1.20</code>
<WRAP center round info 60%>
If you can not login via ssh with failure <code>Unable to negotiate with 192.168.1.20 port 22: no matching host key type found. Their offer: ssh-rsa,ssh-dss
</code>
you have to edit your ssh config like that:
<code>sudo nano /etc/ssh/ssh_config</code>
<code>Host 192.168.1.20
HostKeyAlgorithms ssh-rsa
PubkeyAcceptedKeyTypes ssh-rsa
</code>
Alternatively, you may connect with:
<code>ssh -oHostKeyAlgorithms=+ssh-rsa ubnt@192.168.1.20</code>. If you choose the second method, you will need to pass <code>-oHostKeyAlgorithms=+ssh-rsa</code> to the scp commands as well.
</WRAP>
  - Update the bootloader environment.\\ <code>
fw_setenv devmode TRUE
fw_setenv boot_openwrt "fdt addr \$(fdtcontroladdr); fdt rm /signature; bootubnt"
fw_setenv bootcmd "run boot_openwrt"
</code>
  - At this point you may verify that everything is set correctly. <code>fw_printenv</code>
  - Transfer the OpenWrt sysupgrade image to the device using SCP. <code>scp -O openwrt.bin ubnt@192.168.1.20:/tmp/</code>
  - Check the mtd partition number for bs / kernel0 / kernel1 <code>cat /proc/mtd</code>
  - Set the bootselect (bs) flag to boot from kernel0 <code>dd if=/dev/zero bs=1 count=1 of=/dev/mtdblock4</code>
  - Write the OpenWrt sysupgrade image to both kernel0 as well as kernel1\\ <code>
cd /tmp
dd if=openwrt.bin of=/dev/mtdblock6
dd if=openwrt.bin of=/dev/mtdblock7
</code>
  - Reboot the device. It should boot into OpenWrt.
  - Now system is running in recovery (initramfs) mode, update your firmware with the actual Sysupgrade image.

===== Factory downgrade (preinstallation requirement) =====

  - Connect to the booted device at 192.168.1.20 using username/password "ubnt". <code>ssh ubnt@192.168.1.20</code>
  - Download the old [[https://dl.ubnt.com/unifi/firmware/UAL6/6.0.14.13634/BZ.mt7621_6.0.14+13634.220218.0017.bin|6.0.14 official image]] verified to work and rename it to fwupdate.bin.
  - Transfer the image to the device to path /tmp/fwupdate.bin using SCP. <code>scp -O fwupdate.bin ubnt@192.168.1.20:/tmp/</code>
  - Execute flash using <code>syswrapper.sh upgrade2 &</code>


